  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 4 resealable plastic bags, 4 medium, and 4 mini food storage containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ small pkg fresh mint\n1 English cucumber\n1 pint grape tomatoes"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse chickpeas. Place in a medium bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 (254 g) can garbanzo beans (chickpeas)"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel and mince garlic and shallot. Add both to the bowl with the chickpeas, then mash with a fork or potato masher until smooth.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "garlic\n1 shallot"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, trim, and coarsely grate carrots. Add to the bowl along with eggs, bread crumbs, and spices, then stir to combine. Mash once more until evenly combined.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup panko bread crumbs\n1 tsp coriander, ground\n1 tsp cumin, ground\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp cayenne pepper\n¼ tsp cinnamon, ground"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Roll 2 tablespoons of the chickpea mixture into a ball, then flatten into a 2-inch diameter patty. Place on a plate and repeat with remaining chickpea mixture.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Working in batches if necessary, add chickpea patties and cook until golden and crispy, about 5 minutes per side. Remove to a paper towel-lined plate and set aside to cool completely, about 10 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp extra virgin olive oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, juice lemons into a blender.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Pick mint leaves off the stems; discard stems and add leaves to the blender.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel additional garlic. Add to the blender, along with tahini and salt, then blend on high until smooth, 1-2 minutes. (Add water, a tablespoon at a time, if needed to reach a saucy consistency.) Divide sauce between the mini storage containers and set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "garlic\n½ cup tahini\n½ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Cut pita breads into wedges, then divide between the resealable plastic bags. Store at room temperature until ready to eat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim and slice cucumber crosswise into thin rounds. Halve grape tomatoes. Divide both between the medium containers, along with cooled chickpea patties and mint sauce. Cover and refrigerate until ready to eat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Enjoy chickpea patties, veggies, and pita dipped in sauce.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
